WEBVTT

00:00:00.136 --> 00:00:02.992
Reshaping often happens after joins.

00:00:02.992 --> 00:00:06.607
The danger is that a join can multiply fact rows.

00:00:06.607 --> 00:00:12.122
If you join a patient dimension to admissions, the admission grain can remain intact.

00:00:12.122 --> 00:00:18.297
But joining admissions to another one-to-many child table can create repeated admission combinations.

00:00:18.297 --> 00:00:21.857
Always check cardinality before pivoting joined data.

00:00:21.857 --> 00:00:28.777
A pivot converts category values into columns, usually through conditional aggregation in portable SQL.

00:00:28.777 --> 00:00:32.182
Each target column needs a clear aggregation rule.

00:00:32.182 --> 00:00:37.972
Before pivoting, check whether the source contains more than one value for the same row-key and category

00:00:37.972 --> 00:00:38.720
combination.
